' 22 Allocation job: the names of a new in an Array or a Vector space.
'
' Source of Figure N11.6 in ../design.md (section N11.6). The figure restates
' reified_allocate, allocate_in_spaces, call_authority and allocate_names of
' rholang/src/rust/interpreter/reified/reducer_hooks.rs, the family agent of
' spaces/families.rs and the allocator of spaces/allocator.rs (P5d, F11, P4
' design B.7). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. The reducer draws the names of the new as HEAD does.
'   2. The jobs take the cost authority that the call s!gensym() of the
'      process would carry: the authority of the process, or the cost region
'      of the deploy signature when it is empty, as eval_send stamps a send
'      (P9 step 2).
'   3. One job runs for each distinct space of the plain binders.
'   4. The job takes A(sid) = n, plans the indices, and puts the next value.
'   5. Each binder gets the index name N(sid ‖ u64_be(i)).
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 22-allocation-job.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 22-allocation-job
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor $rrs_relation
  LifeLineBorderColor $rrs_relation
  ParticipantBorderColor $rrs_relation
  GroupBorderColor $rrs_relation
}
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
title Allocation job of a new inside use s (P5d)

participant "Reducer\n(eval_new)" as RED $rrs_host
participant "Reducer hooks" as HOOK $rrs_agent
participant "Family agent" as FAM $rrs_agent
participant "Allocator\n(AllocCx)" as ALC $rrs_agent
participant "SpaceTxn\ncommit" as TXN $rrs_substrate

RED -[$rrs_flow]> HOOK : reified_allocate(new, env, rand, authority)
HOOK -[$rrs_flow]> HOOK : HEAD draws the names of the new
HOOK -[$rrs_relation]> HOOK : call_authority(authority, rand):\nthe authority, or the cost region of the\ndeploy signature when it is empty
loop each distinct space of the plain binders
  HOOK -[$rrs_flow]> FAM : allocate(AllocOp(s, count, rand, call authority))
  FAM -[$rrs_relation]> FAM : read the config once, find the family
  FAM -[$rrs_flow]> ALC : plan(n, count)
  alt OutOfNames
    ALC -[$rrs_fail]> HOOK : abort, nothing staged
  else indices
    ALC -[$rrs_effect]> TXN : take A(sid) = n, put A(sid) = next
    TXN -[$rrs_effect]> HOOK : the indices
  end
end
HOOK -[$rrs_effect]> RED : each binder gets <latex>N(\mathit{sid} \Vert \mathrm{u64\_be}(i))</latex>
@enduml
